WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.517
This comparison is worth learning conceptually.

00:00:02.517 --> 00:00:06.407
GROUPING SETS produces only the grouping combinations you request.

00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:12.252
ROLLUP of A and B produces detail at A and B, a subtotal at A, and a grand total.

00:00:12.252 --> 00:00:17.747
It follows a hierarchy. CUBE of A and B produces detail, subtotals by A, subtotals by B, and the grand total.

00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:22.592
It generates every combination. A simple way to choose is to ask what report levels you need.

00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:26.082
If you need a hierarchy, ROLLUP is often a natural fit.

00:00:26.082 --> 00:00:29.732
If you need all cross-dimensional totals, consider CUBE.

00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:33.152
If you want only specific levels, GROUPING SETS gives you precise control.

00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:39.842
The SQL syntax is different, but the same grain reasoning still applies to every row produced.

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:43.407
Connect this idea to a dashboard summarizing admissions by department and month.

00:00:43.407 --> 00:00:47.997
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:47.997 --> 00:00:53.037
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:53.037 --> 00:00:58.662
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:58.662 --> 00:01:03.397
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
